-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Relationship-derived constraints
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The foreign keys are inline on the columns above; each comment names its relationship (rN in the file of the
-- table). The appendix relationship register gives every one of the 57 relationships a disposition. Summary:
--   * Equal key links (MBA r1, r4, r5, r7, r10, r11, r14, r17, r20, r21, r25, r29; MBS r1, r2, r4, r7, r8, r9, r10,
--     r11, r16, r18, r19, r21, r25, r29, r30, r31; MBS_SendMail r3, r4, r5, r8) -> inline FOREIGN KEY.
--   * Filter links with a constant1 / is_active / is_passed / required predicate (MBA r6, r16, r28; MBS r5, r20, r27,
--     r28, r32; MBS_SendMail r6, r7) -> WHERE clauses in views and queries (BR ids in the appendix).
--   * Context hops that repeat a key link (MBA r8, r15, r18, r19, r23, r24; MBS r12) -> joins.
--   * Name matches (MBS r3 NOMBRE, r6 CURSO, r17 COMPAÑIA = Socio) -> dropped; key links replace them (D-11).
--   * Broken or dead links (MBA r9, r26; MBS r22, r24, r26) -> dropped (D-12, D-16, D-29).

